+## Voyage: empty-edit removal crashes a real browser (browser-only defect)
+
+- Acceptance (Cypress, real browser) fails: "should remove the item if an empty text string was
+  entered" throws `NotFoundError: removeChild ... node no longer a child` from `render`'s
+  stale-list-item removal (`js/app.js:175`), reached through `removeTodo` -> `commitEdit` on the
+  edit keydown. The Cypress advice names a `blur` event handler as the mover.
+- happy-dom cannot reproduce it: a single keydown path removes an attached node cleanly, and
+  happy-dom's own `removeChild` on a detached node throws the same way a real browser does, so no
+  in-suite scenario reddens. Forcing an in-harness failure would be an impossible scenario, so the
+  behaviour is pinned by a source-level `@conformance` check instead.
+- Root cause: `render` removes stale list items with `if (stale.parentNode) stale.parentNode.removeChild(stale)`.
+  A `parentNode` truthiness test is not a connectivity test; in a real browser the edit `blur`
+  handler re-enters `commitEdit`/`render`, so a stale node already detached or moved by the first
+  render reaches a throwing `removeChild`.
+- Pin: `features/edit-removal-safety.feature` carries a `@conformance` scenario that checks the
+  source for an unguarded `removeChild` on a stale list item. It reddens on the current code and
+  greens once the removal is guarded (a connectivity check such as `parentNode.contains(node)` or
+  `node.isConnected`, or the node's own `remove()`).
+- `watchbill.json` `watch1` lists the new scenario plus `edit.feature:An empty edit destroys the todo`
+  as the QM target set for Crew's fix in `js/app.js` (`commitEdit` / `removeTodo` / `render`).
+- Crew fix lives in `js/app.js`; no production code written here.
