+++ b/features/edit-removal-safety.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+Feature: Editing removal safety
+  As a TodoMVC maintainer
+  I want the empty-edit removal to stay safe under a real browser event model
+  So that removing an item on an empty edit does not throw NotFoundError
+
+  Rule: The empty-edit removal must not reach a throwing removeChild on a detached node
+    An empty edit commits its removal through the edit blur handler as well as the keydown
+    handler in a real browser, so render may run twice over the same change. A stale list item
+    that an earlier render already detached or moved must never reach a removeChild that throws
+    NotFoundError, so render may only remove a stale item while it is still attached to its parent.
+
+  @conformance
+  Scenario: The empty-edit removal must not issue an unguarded removeChild
+    Given the app source at "js/app.js"
+    When the verifier checks the edit-commit removal path
+    Then no removeChild is issued on a list item without a connectivity guard
